Perhaps this is just my imagination, as I've often seen this question
asked and never seen this answer given, but...

Sometimes, when you are the HoE/EoB/SSfA, and you _do_ pray
successfully, your god, in addition to solving your immediate
problems, gives you some nifty item:  "An object appears at your
feet!"  It's not an artifact, but it seems to usually be some fairly
nice mundane item:  once I got GoP, the other time a spellbook of
identify.

	-Avrom

PS:  Brunhilde the Valkyrie, my first character to pass the quest and
of whom I wrote the other day, died yesterday.  She had become EoB,
killed Medusa (fell through a trap door and thought to herself
"Wait--didn't I hear that Medusa was around this level?  Better put on
that towel before climbing up the stairs."  Sure enough, Medusa was
waiting right beside the stairs.  Nymphs _are_ good for some things)
and made it to the castle, only to realize I had no musical
instruments, no wands of striking, and no method of levitation.
Couldn't get back up by normal means (as Medusa's sea was in the way),
so I had to #invoke the Orb.  Started searching the dungeon.  Died of
starvation, with Odin displeased.

All my armor was thoroughly damaged/rusty, except my SoR and my
crystal plate mail.  I never saw ONE scroll of
enchant armor in the entire game!!!  I saw 4 amulets of life saving,
all around the necks of monsters.  I got my gold up to a rediculous
amount (for me;  somewhere over 100000) and then had it disappear to a
spellbook.  And with Int/Wis of 17/18, too.  @#$%^&.





